                                 # ONEDRAFT™

## MASTER LICENSING AND INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY FRAMEWORK

**Version 1.0**

### PREAMBLE

OneDraft™ is an AI-native architectural, engineering, and construction drafting platform comprising software, source code, APIs, domain schemas, documentation, artificial-intelligence systems, hosted services, project data structures, technical standards integrations, graphical assets, trademarks, and associated intellectual property.

This Master Licensing and Intellectual Property Framework establishes the licensing structure governing the various components of the OneDraft™ platform.

The purpose of this framework is to preserve an open and extensible technical foundation while establishing appropriate protections and commercial rights for the official OneDraft™ platform, hosted services, proprietary technologies, trademarks, curated data, enterprise capabilities, and other separately designated materials.

No provision of this framework shall be interpreted as converting proprietary materials into open-source materials unless such materials are expressly identified as being released under an applicable open-source license.

---

## PROVISION 1 — DEFINITIONS

For purposes of this Framework:

**“OneDraft™”** means the OneDraft software platform, ecosystem, services, documentation, intellectual property, trademarks, and associated technologies.

**“OneDraft Core”** means the components expressly designated by the project as open-source software and distributed under the Apache License 2.0.

**“OneDraft Platform”** means the broader technical system incorporating OneDraft Core together with additional services, applications, infrastructure, AI systems, proprietary modules, hosted services, and other components.

**“OneDraft Cloud”** means the hosted and managed OneDraft service operated by the official OneDraft provider.

**“OneDraft AI”** means artificial-intelligence orchestration, agent systems, inference infrastructure, model integrations, proprietary prompts, evaluation systems, specialized workflows, and associated technologies designated as proprietary or separately licensed.

**“OneDraft Enterprise”** means commercial enterprise functionality, managed deployments, organizational controls, security features, support services, integrations, and other enterprise offerings.

**“OneDraft Standards”** means curated technical standards, rules, code data, mappings, interpretations, datasets, or other standards-related materials incorporated into or accessed through OneDraft.

**“OneDraft Data”** means user-created project information, project models, drawings, geometry, documentation, and other data submitted to or generated through a OneDraft installation or service.

**“OneDraft Marks”** means the OneDraft™ name, logos, product names, visual identity, service names, and associated trademarks or proposed trademarks.

---

# PROVISION 2 — OPEN-SOURCE CORE LICENSE

The OneDraft Core source code designated by the repository as open source shall be distributed under the **Apache License, Version 2.0**.

The Apache License 2.0 grants applicable recipients rights to use, reproduce, modify, distribute, sublicense, and commercially exploit the licensed source code subject to the terms and conditions of that license.

The complete Apache License 2.0 text shall be provided in the repository's `LICENSE` file.

Where required by the Apache License 2.0, copyright notices, license notices, attribution notices, and applicable NOTICE information shall be preserved.

The Apache License 2.0 applies only to materials expressly designated as being released under that license.

---

# PROVISION 3 — OPEN-SOURCE DOMAIN MODEL AND API

The OneDraft canonical domain model and API components expressly designated as open-source components may be distributed under Apache License 2.0.

Such components may include, as expressly designated:

* canonical domain entities;
* API schemas;
* API specifications;
* SDK interfaces;
* foundational domain libraries;
* interoperability interfaces;
* developer tooling;
* documentation necessary to use the open-source components;
* and other components identified as part of OneDraft Core.

The open-source release does not automatically grant rights to proprietary hosted services, trademarks, proprietary datasets, proprietary AI systems, or separately licensed materials.

---

# PROVISION 4 — COMMERCIAL HOSTED SERVICES

OneDraft Cloud is a commercial service independently offered by the official OneDraft provider.

Access to OneDraft Cloud does not constitute a transfer of ownership of the underlying software, infrastructure, AI systems, proprietary technologies, trademarks, or service infrastructure.

The official provider may offer OneDraft Cloud under free, subscription, usage-based, enterprise, educational, institutional, or other commercial service tiers.

Service pricing, quotas, computational resources, storage, support, availability, and feature access may differ between service tiers.

Access to a free OneDraft Cloud tier does not establish a permanent obligation to provide any particular level of service without charge.

The terms governing hosted services shall be established separately through applicable Terms of Service.

---

# PROVISION 5 — COMMERCIAL LICENSE

Components not expressly released under an open-source license may be made available through a separate commercial license.

A commercial license may authorize specified users or organizations to:

* deploy proprietary OneDraft components;
* operate private instances;
* access enterprise functionality;
* integrate proprietary modules;
* use commercial AI services;
* receive technical support;
* receive managed services;
* obtain service-level commitments;
* and access other capabilities designated by the provider.

Commercial license terms may vary according to deployment type, organization size, usage, territory, support requirements, or other contractual conditions.

---

# PROVISION 6 — SELF-HOSTED DEPLOYMENT

OneDraft may be made available for self-hosted deployment under one or more applicable licenses.

Open-source components may be self-hosted pursuant to their applicable open-source licenses.

Proprietary OneDraft components may require a separate commercial license.

A self-hosted deployment may not use OneDraft Marks in a manner suggesting that the deployment is the official OneDraft service unless expressly authorized.

---

# PROVISION 7 — ONE-DRAFT AI

OneDraft AI components may be divided into open and proprietary components.

Open-source AI-related software released under Apache License 2.0 shall remain subject to that license.

Proprietary AI orchestration, specialized agents, model-routing infrastructure, proprietary evaluation systems, proprietary prompts, private model configurations, inference infrastructure, and other designated technologies may be distributed under separate commercial terms.

Access to an AI service does not necessarily grant ownership of the underlying model, model weights, training data, inference infrastructure, prompts, evaluation datasets, or associated intellectual property.

Third-party AI models and services remain subject to their respective licenses and terms.

---

# PROVISION 8 — THIRD-PARTY MODELS AND DEPENDENCIES

OneDraft may incorporate, interface with, or depend upon third-party software, libraries, models, datasets, fonts, standards, APIs, and other materials.

Such materials are not automatically relicensed under the OneDraft license.

Each third-party component remains subject to its applicable license or contractual terms.

The OneDraft repository shall identify applicable third-party licenses where reasonably required.

---

# PROVISION 9 — PROJECT DATA

Users retain ownership of project data they independently create and submit to OneDraft, subject to applicable third-party rights and contractual terms.

Project data may include:

* requirements;
* project information;
* building models;
* geometry;
* drawings;
* sheets;
* schedules;
* annotations;
* revisions;
* redlines;
* project documents;
* and other user-created materials.

The provision of OneDraft services does not, by itself, transfer ownership of user project data to the OneDraft provider.

The provider may process project data to operate, secure, maintain, and provide the requested OneDraft services in accordance with applicable service terms.

---

# PROVISION 10 — GENERATED OUTPUT

Subject to applicable law, third-party rights, model-provider terms, and the applicable service agreement, users may use project outputs generated through OneDraft for their permitted purposes.

Generated output may include:

* drawings;
* documentation;
* schedules;
* model representations;
* design proposals;
* annotations;
* reports;
* and other project artifacts.

OneDraft does not represent that every generated output is automatically free of third-party intellectual-property rights or regulatory restrictions.

Users remain responsible for reviewing generated technical work before professional, contractual, regulatory, or construction use.

---

# PROVISION 11 — STANDARDS AND CODE INFORMATION

OneDraft Standards may contain or reference information originating from governments, standards organizations, regulatory authorities, publishers, or other third parties.

The inclusion of a CodeSource, CodeRule, or CodeCheck within the OneDraft architecture does not necessarily transfer ownership of the underlying standard or rule to OneDraft.

Third-party standards remain subject to their applicable intellectual-property and licensing conditions.

Where standards require a separate license, subscription, permission, or authorized access mechanism, OneDraft shall not be interpreted as granting such rights.

---

# PROVISION 12 — CODE-AWARE ANALYSIS

OneDraft code-aware functionality is intended to assist users in organizing, evaluating, and reviewing project information against applicable rules and standards.

A CodeCheck or other automated analysis does not, by itself, constitute legal advice, professional certification, regulatory approval, permit approval, or an official determination by an authority having jurisdiction.

Users and qualified professionals remain responsible for determining the applicability and authoritative interpretation of governing requirements.

---

# PROVISION 13 — TRADEMARKS

The names **OneDraft™**, **OneDraft**, associated product names, logos, service names, and other designated marks are separate from the copyright license governing OneDraft source code.

The Apache License 2.0 does not grant a trademark license.

Use of OneDraft Marks in modified, redistributed, hosted, commercial, or derivative products must not create confusion regarding official sponsorship, endorsement, certification, or origin.

A third party may identify compatibility with OneDraft where such identification is truthful and non-misleading, subject to applicable trademark law and any published trademark policy.

The official OneDraft service may reserve the exclusive right to use the OneDraft Marks in connection with official products and services.

---

# PROVISION 14 — CONTRIBUTOR LICENSE

Contributions to OneDraft Core may be accepted under the applicable contribution terms established by the project.

A contributor must have the necessary rights to submit the contribution.

Unless otherwise agreed in writing, contributions intended for OneDraft Core shall be licensed under the same open-source license applicable to the relevant project component.

The project may require a Contributor License Agreement or equivalent contribution terms for certain repositories or components.

---

# PROVISION 15 — COMMERCIAL EXTENSIONS

Commercial extensions may be developed independently of OneDraft Core.

Commercial extensions may include:

* enterprise administration;
* advanced collaboration;
* proprietary AI capabilities;
* managed cloud infrastructure;
* specialized rendering;
* advanced standards integrations;
* private model integrations;
* enterprise identity systems;
* specialized analysis;
* professional support systems;
* and other proprietary capabilities.

Commercial extensions are not automatically subject to the Apache License 2.0 merely because they interface with OneDraft Core.

The licensing status of each extension shall be expressly identified.

---

# PROVISION 16 — OPEN-CORE COMPATIBILITY

OneDraft is intended to support an open-core ecosystem.

The existence of commercially licensed components does not restrict the rights granted by the Apache License 2.0 to independently licensed OneDraft Core components.

Likewise, the open-source release of OneDraft Core does not require proprietary OneDraft services or independently developed commercial extensions to be released under Apache License 2.0, except where applicable copyright, derivative-work, dependency, or other legal requirements establish otherwise.

---

# PROVISION 17 — API ACCESS

Public APIs designated as open-source or publicly documented may be used according to their published terms.

Commercial APIs, hosted inference APIs, enterprise APIs, metered services, or restricted interfaces may be subject to separate usage terms.

API credentials are not transferable unless expressly authorized.

Automated access may be subject to rate limits, usage limits, security controls, and service-specific restrictions.

---

# PROVISION 18 — ENTERPRISE LICENSING

Enterprise customers may obtain additional rights through written commercial agreements.

Enterprise agreements may address:

* private deployment;
* data residency;
* security requirements;
* service-level commitments;
* support;
* integration;
* identity management;
* dedicated infrastructure;
* confidential processing;
* audit requirements;
* and other organizational requirements.

Where a written enterprise agreement conflicts with a general service term, the negotiated agreement shall govern to the extent expressly stated.

---

# PROVISION 19 — EDUCATIONAL AND RESEARCH USE

OneDraft may be offered under special educational or research programs.

Such programs may provide free or reduced-cost access to commercial services while retaining the applicable ownership and licensing structure.

Open-source components remain available under their applicable open-source licenses.

---

# PROVISION 20 — DATA AND PRIVACY

OneDraft services may process information necessary to provide requested functionality.

The provider shall establish separate privacy terms governing the collection, processing, retention, security, and deletion of personal information.

Users should not submit information to OneDraft services unless they have the authority to provide and process such information.

Additional enterprise data-processing agreements may apply where required.

---

# PROVISION 21 — SECURITY

OneDraft implementations shall employ reasonable technical and organizational measures appropriate to the deployment and sensitivity of the applicable environment.

Security-sensitive components may be distributed separately from general open-source components.

Disclosure of security vulnerabilities should follow the project's published security reporting process.

---

# PROVISION 22 — NO AUTOMATIC PROFESSIONAL AUTHORITY

OneDraft is software and does not itself become an architect, engineer, contractor, regulator, authority having jurisdiction, standards organization, or other professional authority merely by generating or analyzing project information.

Professional responsibility for design, engineering, code interpretation, construction documentation, certification, permitting, and construction remains subject to the applicable professional and regulatory framework.

---

# PROVISION 23 — NO WARRANTY THROUGH OPEN-SOURCE LICENSE

Open-source OneDraft components distributed under Apache License 2.0 are provided according to the warranty and liability provisions of that license.

Commercial services may be subject to separate warranty, service-level, support, limitation-of-liability, and indemnification provisions established through applicable commercial agreements.

---

# PROVISION 24 — LICENSE VERSIONING

The licensing designation of each OneDraft repository or component shall be expressly identified.

A future version of OneDraft may introduce additional licenses, dual licensing, commercial licensing, or revised licensing arrangements for newly created components.

A change in the licensing of future releases shall not retroactively revoke rights already granted under an applicable open-source license.

---

# PROVISION 25 — SEPARABILITY OF COMPONENT LICENSES

The OneDraft ecosystem may contain components governed by different licenses.

For clarity:

**OneDraft Core**
Apache License 2.0.

**OneDraft Cloud**
Commercial service terms.

**OneDraft Enterprise**
Commercial license and/or enterprise agreement.

**OneDraft AI proprietary components**
Commercial or proprietary license as designated.

**Third-party dependencies**
Their respective licenses.

**Standards and regulatory data**
Applicable third-party rights and licenses.

**OneDraft Marks**
Separate trademark rights.

**User Project Data**
Owned or controlled by the applicable user or rights holder, subject to applicable agreements and law.

---

# PROVISION 26 — COMMERCIAL BUSINESS MODEL

OneDraft may generate revenue through multiple independent channels without restricting the rights granted to the open-source OneDraft Core.

Commercial offerings may include:

**OneDraft Cloud** — hosted subscription services.

**OneDraft Pro** — professional design and documentation capabilities.

**OneDraft Team** — collaborative project environments.

**OneDraft Enterprise** — enterprise deployment, administration, security, and support.

**OneDraft Private** — private or self-hosted commercial deployments.

**OneDraft AI** — metered or subscription-based AI computation and specialized intelligence.

**OneDraft API** — usage-based API access.

**OneDraft Services** — implementation, integration, training, support, and professional services.

The commercial model may evolve independently of the open-source core.

---

# PROVISION 27 — OFFICIAL DISTRIBUTION

The official OneDraft distribution shall be identified through designated project repositories, official domains, release signatures, package identifiers, or other verification mechanisms.

Third-party distributions may exist and may be legally permitted under applicable open-source licenses.

Third-party distributions shall not automatically constitute official OneDraft releases.

---

# PROVISION 28 — GOVERNANCE

The OneDraft project may establish separate governance for:

* open-source development;
* commercial product development;
* security;
* standards integration;
* trademark administration;
* community contributions;
* and enterprise services.

Governance structures may evolve as the project develops.

---

# PROVISION 29 — COPYRIGHT AND NOTICE

Copyright notices contained within OneDraft source files, documentation, or other protected materials shall be preserved as required by the applicable license.

Nothing in this Framework transfers ownership of intellectual property except where expressly stated in a written agreement.

---

# PROVISION 30 — INTERPRETATION

This Framework is intended to establish the licensing architecture of OneDraft™.

Where a specific component contains its own `LICENSE`, `NOTICE`, terms of service, commercial agreement, or other governing instrument, that instrument shall control the licensing of that component to the extent applicable.

The open-source license applicable to OneDraft Core shall remain distinct from commercial service terms, trademark rights, third-party intellectual-property rights, and user-owned project data.

---

# PROVISION 31 — LICENSE HIERARCHY

The intended OneDraft licensing hierarchy is:

```text
                         ONEDRAFT™
                             │
          ┌──────────────────┼──────────────────┐
          │                  │                  │
     OPEN SOURCE         COMMERCIAL          THIRD PARTY
          │                  │                  │
    Apache 2.0          Service Terms      Their License
          │                  │                  │
    OneDraft Core       Cloud / Enterprise    Libraries
    Domain / API        AI / API / Support    Models
    SDK / Tooling       Private Deployment    Standards
          │                  │                  │
          └──────────────────┼──────────────────┘
                             │
                       USER PROJECT DATA
                             │
                      User-Controlled Data
```

This hierarchy is intended to permit broad adoption of the open technical foundation while preserving sustainable commercial opportunities around hosted services, proprietary technologies, enterprise capabilities, and the OneDraft brand.

---

# PROVISION 32 — EFFECTIVE LICENSING STRUCTURE

Unless expressly designated otherwise:

**OneDraft Core:** Apache License 2.0.

**OneDraft Cloud:** Commercial service.

**OneDraft Pro:** Commercial service/license.

**OneDraft Team:** Commercial service/license.

**OneDraft Enterprise:** Commercial license/agreement.

**OneDraft Private:** Commercial deployment license where proprietary components are included.

**OneDraft AI proprietary infrastructure:** Commercial/proprietary license.

**Public APIs:** License or API terms designated for the applicable API.

**Third-party software:** Applicable third-party license.

**Standards and code databases:** Applicable third-party licensing terms.

**User Project Data:** User-controlled, subject to applicable agreements and law.

**OneDraft™ trademarks and branding:** Reserved separately from the software copyright license.

---

# PROVISION 33 — FINAL STATEMENT

OneDraft™ is intended to establish an open technical foundation for intelligent CAD/BIM while maintaining a sustainable commercial ecosystem capable of supporting continued engineering, infrastructure, artificial-intelligence development, standards integration, security, hosting, research, and enterprise deployment.

The licensing architecture therefore distinguishes between **open software**, **commercial services**, **proprietary technology**, **third-party materials**, **user data**, and **trademark rights**.

The objective is not to restrict the development of the OneDraft ecosystem.

The objective is to allow the ecosystem to grow while preserving a viable official OneDraft platform capable of funding the continued development of the technology.

**OneDraft™**

**Open Core. Intelligent Platform. Commercial Ecosystem.**
